<title>GREECE: Michaniki trades ex-div May 21.</title>
<headline>Michaniki trades ex-div May 21.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of construction firm Michaniki traded ex-dividend on Wednesday after shareholders approved the fiscal 1996 dividend during Tuesday's assembly.</p>
<p>Michaniki will pay a net dividend per share of 150 drachmas.</p>
<p>Management told shareholders it expects group turnover to rise to 33.8 billion drachmas this year and hit 43.1 billion in 1998.</p>
<p>Pretax profit is forecast to grow to 6.78 billion this year and 9.7 billion in 1998. The company posted pretax earnings of 5.02 billion drachmas in 1996, a growth of 24 percent. --George Georgiopoulos, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
</text>
